<title>USA: Boeing delivered 92 commercial jets in Q2.</title>
<headline>Boeing delivered 92 commercial jets in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co said Monday it delivered 92 commercial jets in the second quarter.</p>
<p>The deliveries included 35 737s, 12 747s, 12 757s, 12 767s and 21 777s.</p>
<p>The company said it has delivered a total of 160 jets in the first six months of the year, including 60 737s, 22 747s, 24 757s, 23 767s and 31 777s. In addition, one non-commercial 767 was delivered in the first quarter.</p>
<p>Boeing said it continues to project total 1997 deliveries to be in the 340-airplane range.</p>
</text>
